Layout is a special type used for layouts. The function returning a Layout must <~
take a Renderable (View, Layout or Island) as an argument and use it in the HTML it outputs. <~
expose is the equivalent of "export" in JS, and "public" in other languages. <~
If a layout is going to be used outside the filesystem-based router, it has to be exposed. <~
expose Layout HtmlShell(Renderable children) {
    return <html>
    <head>...</head>

    <body>
        {children}
    </body>
    </html>
}
